-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

None are reproduced here, and that is a statement about how this repository is
distributed rather than an omission. Nothing is vendored: every dependency in
requirements.txt and the four optional extras is resolved from PyPI at install
time, so their licences travel with the wheels pip fetches rather than with this
source tree.

The sibling Motrix Edge View repository does carry a third-party list, because its
single-file build inlines its dependencies into the artifact it publishes. That
is the condition that would change this section: ship an image or an archive
with dependencies baked in, and their notices have to travel with it.
